{
  "action": "hold_drawer_key",
  "note": "Eight seconds on the red lamp. Phil is already on the wire copy, reading the same flat weather string he'll read every morning. I want the ident. My brother's voice, the one where he calls me Mercury and I forget to cut the mic — that's the sound of this station, not a wire feed. The vermilion tin is sealed in the drawer and the combination is mine, 5066. I pocket the key. Phil's booth access is gone for the shift. The archive is mine; the broadcast will be local, or it won't be mine at all. I'll let the tape breathe before the next segment. Eight seconds is enough to take the key and turn the red lamp over to my side of the board."
}
